# Local dev-stand overlay: the compose override that keeps the stand's data
# volumes across `down` (see dev/stand/README.md). Machine-specific by nature —
# ports, volume paths and which engines a given box runs — so it is never
# committed. Its absence is what makes the tracked docker-compose.yaml the
# single reproducible definition.
/docker-compose.override.yaml

# downloaded previous-release binary — the release gate's regression baseline
/.gate-baseline/

# Cross-compilation target dirs. `cargo` only ever ignores `target/` itself, so
# a build driven with `--target-dir target-linux` (e.g. `docker run ... cargo
# build --target-dir /w/target-amd64` when producing a Linux binary from a Mac)
# lands 7.5k files and ~1.2 GB per arch INSIDE the crate — where `cargo
# package` would happily pick them up. This covers the `target-<arch>` naming
# the accident used (2ed9548b, 7546 files) and the sibling shapes cargo users
# reach for; it does NOT cover every conceivable build dir (`build-linux/`,
# `linux-target/`, `target_amd64/` are all still visible to `git add -A`).
# Enumerating names cannot close that — the general case is guarded by CONTENT
# in .githooks/pre-commit, which refuses a commit that stages .rlib/.rmeta/
# fingerprint/incremental paths or an implausible number of files.
/target-*/
.mutants-cache/

# Claude instructions live in ~/.claude (private), never in the public tree.
CLAUDE.md
CLAUDE.local.md
